---
// The Findish wordmark: the name in Atkinson bold, with "dish" sitting in a shallow nori
// bowl, so it reads as find + dish (a solid half-round with a flat rim, not a curved line, so it reads as a bowl and not a smile). Pure text and CSS: it scales with the font size it's
// given, follows light and dark mode, and screen readers hear one word, "Findish".
---

<span class="wordmark">Fin<span class="wordmark-dish">dish</span></span>

<style>
  .wordmark {
    display: inline-block;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .wordmark-dish {
    position: relative;
    display: inline-block;
    padding-inline: 0.02em 0.04em;
  }

  /* The bowl: a solid half-round with a flat rim, under "dish", in the one accent color.
     Decoration only; the letters sit just above its rim. */
  .wordmark-dish::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline: -0.04em 0;
    bottom: -0.2em;
    height: 0.2em;
    background: var(--accent-ink);
    border-radius: 0.02em 0.02em 50% 50% / 0.02em 0.02em 100% 100%;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    .wordmark-dish::after {
      background: CanvasText;
    }
  }
</style>
